{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3087","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3087","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3087\",\"parent_revision\":\"be31811e12e1c7388c85902b55c477f29a476c49077e449f5881de80333079f4\",\"root_revision\":\"be31811e12e1c7388c85902b55c477f29a476c49077e449f5881de80333079f4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-20\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`get-gate-token.mjs` generates a new random token and overwrites the session's single `.gate-token` file on every invocation; `backlog_core/server.py`'s `_read_gate_token()` validates a caller's `gate_token` only against the file's current contents. A token obtained by an earlier call in a session becomes invalid the moment anything else in that session regenerates the file \u2014 including a concurrent subagent reloading the `work-backlog-item` skill, or a later step in the same logical flow \u2014 causing a legitimate `backlog_add` call to be spuriously rejected as unauthorized.\\n\\nSeparately, and already documented as a known/accepted gap in `create/start.md` Step 4: `gate_token` only gates the MCP `backlog_add` tool, not the CLI path or raw GitHub API calls, so it does not universally enforce skill-mediated creation. This item is not about that already-accepted gap \u2014 it is about the rotation defect above, which affects legitimate MCP-path callers.\\n\\nSurfaced during review of ADR-3075-4 (`plugins/development-harness/docs/adrs/`), where `gate_token` was mistakenly proposed as a session-identity mechanism for an unrelated cache-routing decision \u2014 its actual purpose is access gating for `backlog_add`, not carrying stable session identity. That mismatch prompted the question of whether `gate_token`'s current design (single rotating token file per session) still serves its actual goal reliably, or should be redesigned or removed.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **gate_token's rotating single-file design causes spurious rejection within one session** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8eeb7ee5e8f2f9b85f59f199413d65ee7548b252445888f2ef420283ea943700\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABP84-YA\"}"}